<title>LUXEMBOURG: Waigel, Strauss-Kahn have no comment at EU meeting.</title>
<headline>Waigel, Strauss-Kahn have no comment at EU meeting.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-06-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel and his French counterpart Dominique Strauss-Kahn had little to say as they entered a European Union finance ministers meeting on Sunday.</p>
<p>Waigel, in the eye of the storm over German plans to revalue its gold reserves, said nothing at all.</p>
<p>Strauss-Kahn said only that discussion of the French Socialist government's views would have wait until Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;You'll see tomorrow,&quot; he told reporters.</p>
</text>
